From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:32:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 168/168] PC5: an effect's OnResetDevice succeeds (Wine patch
 1039)

ID3DXEffect::OnResetDevice answered E_NOTIMPL. A game that resets its device when it switches to fullscreen and checks what its effects answer took that as a failed reset and stopped drawing: its screen stayed black right after the switch, and it drew only in a window, where there is no reset. Microsoft's d3dx9_43.dll answers D3D_OK. Wine's effect has nothing of the device's to make again after a reset (OnLostDevice only lets go of default-pool textures set as parameters, which the application sets again), so it answers D3D_OK too.
---
 ...9-an-effect-s-onresetdevice-succeeds.patch | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1039-d3dx9-an-effect-s-onresetdevice-succeeds.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1039-d3dx9-an-effect-s-onresetdevice-succeeds.patch b/wine/patches/1039-d3dx9-an-effect-s-onresetdevice-succeeds.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..02a44d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1039-d3dx9-an-effect-s-onresetdevice-succeeds.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:40:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] d3dx9: An effect's OnResetDevice succeeds.
+
+ID3DXEffect::OnResetDevice was a stub answering E_NOTIMPL. A game that
+resets its device when it switches to fullscreen, and checks what its
+effects answer, took that as a failed reset and stopped drawing: WRC
+Powerslide's screen stayed black right after the switch, with Auto as
+with WineD3D, and drew in a window, where there is no reset. Microsoft's
+d3dx9_43.dll answers D3D_OK, and with it the game got past the switch.
+
+OnLostDevice only lets go of the D3DPOOL_DEFAULT textures set as the
+effect's parameters, which the application sets again after the reset,
+so the effect has nothing of the device's to make again: it answers
+D3D_OK.
+---
+ dlls/d3dx9_36/effect.c | 9 +++++----
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/d3dx9_36/effect.c b/dlls/d3dx9_36/effect.c
+index a8eeca4..fb34bba 100644
+--- a/dlls/d3dx9_36/effect.c
++++ b/dlls/d3dx9_36/effect.c
+@@ -4200,11 +4200,12 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI d3dx_effect_OnLostDevice(ID3DXEffect *iface)
+ 
+ static HRESULT WINAPI d3dx_effect_OnResetDevice(ID3DXEffect *iface)
+ {
+-    struct d3dx_effect *This = impl_from_ID3DXEffect(iface);
+-
+-    FIXME("(%p)->(): stub\n", This);
++    TRACE("iface %p.\n", iface);
+ 
+-    return E_NOTIMPL;
++    /* OnLostDevice only lets go of the D3DPOOL_DEFAULT textures set as
++     * parameters, which the application sets again after the reset; the
++     * effect holds nothing else of the device's to make again. */
++    return D3D_OK;
+ }
+ 
+ static HRESULT WINAPI d3dx_effect_SetStateManager(ID3DXEffect *iface, ID3DXEffectStateManager *manager)
-- 
